=== SURVEY ===
Web source AnnouncerRegion.tsx is the global screen-reader announcer mount point. It renders TWO
visually-hidden live regions (one polite, one assertive) — kept as siblings so each region's
aria-live value stays static — and subscribes via `subscribeAnnouncer((message, priority) => …)`,
routing each message into the matching region's state. The two regions are the entire output;
there is no visible UI and NO `t()` call (the surface is anonymous).
Backing module web/src/hooks/useAnnouncer.ts:
  • `announce(message, priority='polite')` — empty messages skipped; a module counter is bumped and
    the message is suffixed with `'\u200B'.repeat(announceCounter % 4)` (rotating zero-width spaces)
    so screen readers re-read identical consecutive messages; the padded string is pushed to every
    subscribed region.
  • `subscribeAnnouncer(listener)` → returns an unsubscribe closure; calls made before any region
    mounts are dropped (no listeners) — mirroring the assistive-tech reality.
VisuallyHidden.tsx: liveRegion polite → role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic; assertive →
role="alert" aria-live="assertive" aria-atomic.
Data sources (P1/S8): useAnnouncer. Shared components: none. Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys extracted from source: none (anonymous surface — reproduce regions from source).
Existing native: no Announcer/AnnouncerRegion/AnnouncerPriority/AnnouncementPresenter symbols
(no collision). `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_).post()` already used in-repo
(Sources/App/AppShell.swift, feature-views/WidgetPicker.swift) → the native voicing API is valid here.
Canonical surface pattern studied: misc-surfaces/globalShortcuts + TourLauncher
(Adapter/Model/Seams/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests/ModelTests).

=== REASONING ===
- The web component renders nothing visible (two sr-only regions); the prompt requires a
  production-polished native surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and (native-chrome)
  i18n, with every state visible (no blank box). Chosen: a native "announcements inspector" — the
  two live regions presented visibly (Polite + Assertive cards, each naming its role + current
  message) over a recent-announcement log — while performing the REAL assistive-tech voicing
  (AccessibilityNotification) so the underlying aria-live contract is reproduced, not just drawn.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical globalShortcuts/TourLauncher leaf:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AnnouncerPriority (web 'polite'|'assertive' → interrupting flag),
    AnnouncerMessage (id=web announceCounter, clean text + padded announcementText), AnnouncerPadding
    (verbatim port of the `announceCounter % 4` zero-width-space dedupe), AnnouncerRegionAccessibility.
  • Model: AnnouncerTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; AnnouncementPresenter seam
    (native voicing boundary) + OSLog default; AnnouncerConnection axis; AnnouncerRegionInput snapshot
    (derives latest polite/assertive = web component state); AnnouncerRegionResolved + Projection
    (loading/empty/error/data); @Observable AnnouncerRegionModel (binds the source, posts each new
    message once via the presenter, one-shot stale auto-refresh); AnnouncerRegionStrings i18n facade.
  • Seams: Announcer (the native port of the useAnnouncer module — subscriber set + rotating dedupe
    counter, drops pre-subscription calls), AnnouncerSubscription, AnnouncerRegionSource protocol,
    LiveAnnouncerRegionSource (bridges the announcer stream into bounded snapshots),
    InMemoryAnnouncerRegionSource (previews/tests), AccessibilityAnnouncementPresenter (posts a real
    AccessibilityNotification.Announcement carrying the iOS18/macOS15 speech-priority attribute:
    assertive → .high interrupts, polite → .default queues).
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton region cards), empty (no announcements voiced yet — friendly
  TSEmptyState, never blank), error (retry — web QueryError peer), data (two regions + recent log),
  and the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the
  stale transition).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/sr-only literally (native has no aria-live — used the platform
  AccessibilityNotification instead, the idiomatic equivalent); a truly invisible surface (the P4
  leaf contract forbids blank boxes — rendered the regions visibly as an inspector); direct posting
  from the view (routed through the presenter seam so the voicing is unit-testable); HTTP in the
  view (bound via the source seam).
- Build inclusion (necessary infra, documented): TeslaSync/shared-surfaces was NOT yet a source dir
  in project.yml nor in .swiftlint.yml `included`. Both were wired (mirroring feature-views /
  dashboard-widgets / misc-surfaces) so the gate actually COMPILES + LINTS this surface — without it
  the gate would pass vacuously over zero of my files (that would itself be red-as-green). Idempotent
  and mergeable with sibling shared-surfaces prompts (0002 RouteAnnouncer, 0003 VisuallyHidden, …).

